1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
Every truck leaving a container terminal passes a gate.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,667
Five systems describe each box, and they often disagree.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,259
On a bad night the gate closes,

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:13,704
and every truck in line pays in delay, fees, and idling diesel.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,815
This is Rung at Pier 7, on an ordinary Tuesday. 191 boxes wait.

6
00:00:19,815 --> 00:00:26,111
Rung reads five sources per box and puts each on the gentlest safe step of this ladder,

7
00:00:26,111 --> 00:00:29,074
from Release to Hand, where a person decides.

8
00:00:29,074 --> 00:00:30,556
34 need a planner.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,852
This box needs an answer.

10
00:00:32,852 --> 00:00:34,704
The manifest says 36,000 pounds.

11
00:00:34,704 --> 00:00:37,667
The scale says 40,500, a 12.5 percent gap.

12
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:39,889
Rung does not guess. It asks.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,704
Its voice agent, built on Retell AI, calls the trucker.

14
00:00:46,704 --> 00:00:50,037
This video plays the simulated version of that call,

15
00:00:50,037 --> 00:00:52,630
so it runs the same every time.

16
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:54,481
The trucker backs the scale.

17
00:00:54,481 --> 00:00:57,074
Rung still will not pick a side.

18
00:00:57,074 --> 00:01:00,407
The box goes to Hand, and a planner decides.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,963
This is the exact prompt that agent runs,

20
00:01:04,963 --> 00:01:08,667
read from the setup script that creates it in Retell.

21
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:13,481
Who it is, how to say a container number, the weight check steps,

22
00:01:13,481 --> 00:01:16,444
and the only four outcomes it may record.

23
00:01:16,444 --> 00:01:18,296
The model runs the conversation.

24
00:01:18,296 --> 00:01:20,519
Rung's rules decide what happens next.

25
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,333
Now the worst night of the year, Harbor Night.

26
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:28,185
Lanes 4 to 6 close.

27
00:01:28,185 --> 00:01:33,370
Rung re-plans every truck in under a millisecond and keeps 96 of 129 moving.

28
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,593
Closing the terminal would keep none.

29
00:01:35,593 --> 00:01:38,926
Customs drops a new hold on a dry box.

30
00:01:38,926 --> 00:01:41,148
Then the terminal feed goes dark.

31
00:01:41,148 --> 00:01:47,074
By our model, Rung saves about 90 idle truck hours and over 700 kilograms of CO2.

32
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,963
The queue now lists what went wrong tonight.

33
00:01:52,963 --> 00:01:58,148
With the feed dark, Rung does not hand a hundred boxes to a person.

34
00:01:58,148 --> 00:02:01,481
Only the 21 trucks due now go to Hand.

35
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,593
This box cannot wait, and cannot go.

36
00:02:05,593 --> 00:02:09,667
Chilled beef, power off since nine, already past its loss limit,

37
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:11,148
under a customs hold.

38
00:02:11,148 --> 00:02:13,741
Releasing it is not ours to give.

39
00:02:13,741 --> 00:02:18,185
Rung says Hold, names the customs broker, and attaches the reefer evidence.

40
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,704
Every step, call, and override lands in the audit log,

41
00:02:23,704 --> 00:02:25,926
with its reason in plain words.

42
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,593
Rung is not tied to one port.

43
00:02:29,593 --> 00:02:34,778
Switch to Rotterdam and the same engine speaks kilograms, euros, Dutch customs, and Portbase.

44
00:02:34,778 --> 00:02:36,259
Same rules, same decisions.

45
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,481
Rules decide. People sign.

46
00:02:38,481 --> 00:02:43,296
Rung, built with Retell AI, the Terminal49 data model, FastAPI, React, and SciPy.

47
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:45,148
Next, NSF SBIR Phase One.
